  <questionvariables><text><![CDATA[/* Fixed: any right-angled triangle with the right angle at A or C scores. */
ta1: 3; ta2: 5; ta3: 4;
/* The numerical input type alone accepts %i, inf, sets, lists, booleans and equations: this validator keeps them from the PRT. */
validate_real(ex) := block([sv, fv], sv: ev(ex, simp), fv: errcatch(ev(bfloat(sv), simp)), if ratnump(sv) then "" else if is(fv = []) then "Enter a single real number, for example 3, -1/2 or sqrt(2)." else if bfloatp(first(fv)) then "" else "Enter a single real number, for example 3, -1/2 or sqrt(2).");
/* True when u is positive. Exact for a rational number. Otherwise bigfloats (float() overflows on very large lengths), and a value below 10^(-40) of the scale sz counts as zero, so that a zero typed in a form that does not simplify, such as sin(1)^2 + cos(1)^2 - 1, is not taken for a tiny positive length. */
ispos(u, sz) := block([rr, fpprec: 60], rr: ev(trigsimp(ratsimp(radcan(u))), simp), if ratnump(rr) then is(rr > 0) else is(bfloat(rr) > 10^(-40)*sz));
/* True when u^2 + v^2 = w^2. Exact whenever the difference simplifies to a rational number. A form that does not simplify exactly is compared with 60-digit bigfloats, to 10^(-40) of w^2. */
pythag(u, v, w) := block([rr, fpprec: 60], rr: ev(trigsimp(ratsimp(radcan(u^2 + v^2 - w^2))), simp), if ratnump(rr) then is(rr = 0) else is(abs(bfloat(rr)) < 10^(-40)*bfloat(w^2)));]]></text></questionvariables>
